  "notes": {
    "folders": "empty on purpose: this site's prefixes are written with a dash (cv-in, lp-hero), and `folders` only expands folder_element names (one underscore), so every class is an explicit rename. The fp-X-Y entries are the image focal-point utility system (see below).",
    "fp-X-Y": "object-position X% Y% on an image (`.fp-50-50.fp-50-50 {object-position: 50% 50%}`), a generated 11x11 grid: renamed as the property-family utility object-position-X-Y, all 121 of them (25 used, 96 only in the registry's selectors) so the system stays complete.",
    "wrap / wrap--wide": "two content widths: width min(var(--wrap), 100% - 2 gutters) and min(96rem, …). wrap--wide is used on its own, never stacked on wrap, so it is a second container utility, not a combo.",
    "chapter-tag / kicker": "both are the small uppercase gold label above headings: chapter-tag (369 uses, an <i> line before it) is the tagline role; kicker (126 uses, a ::before line, in 'Where next', 'Related', 'In their words') becomes text-style-label. Merge candidate once one line technique is chosen.",
    "lead / small / serif / display / h2 / h3": "type roles: h2, h3 and display are heading looks on non-heading tags (custom elements), lead is the intro paragraph style (size + muted colour + measure), serif is the display font on quotes and numbers.",
    "num": "the gold '01, 02 …' index inside cards and lists; only styled in context (.cp-col-head .num, .lg-list .num …).",
    "btn-gold / btn-ghost": "gold fill = is-primary, outline = is-secondary (btn carries one of them everywhere it is used).",
    "magnetic": "no styles: the hook site.js uses for the magnetic hover. Named as a state combo; a data- attribute is the standard's next step.",
    "textlink / arrow": "the underlined uppercase link with a → that slides on hover; arrow is the → span, also used on the 'next page' cards.",
    "frame": "the media frame (overflow hidden, tinted ground) every photo sits in; frame--tall / frame--wide set 4:5 and 16:9.",
    "par": "the parallax image inside a frame (site.js selects '.par' and moves it); cv-pos is the cover image hook (no styles).",
    "full": "a form label that spans both columns of the consultation form grid (.in-fields label.full).",
    "bar": "the progress bar inside the nav section readout ('Arrival ——').",
    "is-lp": "on <body> of the six landing pages; already a combo shape but 'lp' is an abbreviation.",
    "b-": "b- = page BLOCK: every b-<name> is a section and becomes section_<name>; its two-letter prefix becomes the folder: cv cover, st statement, sp steps, cp compare, ph photo strip, lg ledger (numbered reasons list), ba before/after (b-proof), rl card rail, ga gallery, sy stories, vd videos, tm team, dt detail, px post index, pl place (location), pr2 prose, fq faq, tb tabs.",
    "b-proof": "named section_before-after, not section_proof: its content is the pinned before/after slider (ba-*); the home page 'proof' (reviews marquee) is ch-proof.",
    "ch-": "home page chapters (arrival, reality, answer, precision, surgeon, transformation, experience, invitation); ch-proof is a div inside ch-experience, so it is proof_component, not a section. ch-invitation is the contact + form block at the foot of 80 pages.",
    "an-": "the 'Not sure which is right for you?' horizontal track of six answer cards on the home page.",
    "lp-": "lp- = the ads landing pages. lp-cz = consultation page hero (form), lp-ty = thank-you hero, lp-why = reasons, lp-journey (lp-jr, lp-beats) = one patient's before/after journey, lp-proof = doctor + quotes, lp-cards = 'what the call covers', lp-proto = the GHL form placeholder, lp-slot its embed slot.",
    "dt-light / lp-cards--light / ph-light": "paper (light) colour scheme on a dark site. dt-light is a standalone section style → section-style-light; lp-cards--light is a combo → is-light. ph-light only appears in selectors (no element carries it): left out.",
    "--modifiers": "every BEM modifier (x--y) becomes an is- combo: --split, --bleed, --small, --tall, --wide, --after, --text, --mirror, --doctor, --emily, --michael (per-photo focal tweaks), --band, --hero, --cz (consultation/thank-you title size).",
    "LEFT OUT": "wz-* and reveal-mask (runtime classes added by the Webzite kit / SplitText), elfsight-app-… (third-party widget class), and selectors that match nothing on the site (frame--sq, ph-light, sy-ba, rule: delete-candidates).",
    "MERGE CANDIDATES (audit, identical declarations; not merged here)": "ga-head = sy-head = vd-head = tm-head = px-head = lp-cards-head; ar-bg = ex-bg = cv-bg = lp-hero-bg; b-cover = lp-hero = lp-cz = lp-ty; ch-answer = b-steps = b-rail; ba-before = ga-before = lp-ba-before; pl-photo = lp-why-shot = lp-proof-shot; frame--wide = pr-shot; ar-film = cv-film; ar-veil = cv-veil; ar-lead = cv-lead; ar-actions = cv-actions; ch-reality = b-statement. Also the three before/after sliders (ba-, ga-, lp-ba-) are one component in three copies.",
    "lp-form": "2026-10-08: the GHL campaign-form Embed block inside the landing form slot (.lp-slot .lp-form), added 2026-10-05 by add-ghl-forms.mjs.",
    "in-ghl": "2026-10-08: the GHL contact/referral Embed block in every Invitation chapter card (apply-ghl-site-forms.mjs, seq 36).",
    "st-services": "2026-10-08: nav.st-services, the Dental Implants services list beside the statement on /dental-implants (BugHerd #38); its label is st-services-k.",
    "scriptClassCalls": "2026-10-08: the draft-patch scripts in workflows/21-instatic-upload select nodes with hasClass(node, <class>) and rules with ruleByName(<class>); renamed with the same map in --files mode."
  },
  "scriptClassCalls": [
    "hasClass",
    "ruleByName"
  ]
}
